IMPLEMENTATION (parity with the web source; native primitives + P1/S9 tokens, no Tailwind ports):
  - Self-fetching surface (SessionComparisonChart pattern): own cache-then-network source over
    GET /analytics/cost-forecast?vehicle_id=&months=6 (op get_api_v1_analytics_cost_forecast), so the
    surface renders the full P2 state matrix (loading skeleton / loaded / empty / error retry /
    stale chip / offline chip) the web prop-fed child cannot. No HTTP in the view.
  - Two cost panels reproduced: (1) forecast TsComposedChart = Actual Cost area (historical) +
    95% Confidence area (forecast cost_high upper envelope) + Projected Cost line (forecast cost),
    web hasForecast gate (historical>=3 && forecast>0), needData empty branch; (2) cost-per-kWh
    TsLineChart over historical cost_per_kwh, web hasCostPerKwhTrend gate (historical>1), needTrendData
    empty branch. Categorical month axis surfaced as a month-label strip (web XAxis dataKey=month).
  - Confidence band note: web stacks ci_low+ci_band; the native cartesian surface fills areas to the
    zero baseline (no stacking), so the band is drawn as the upper bound (cost_high) envelope with the
    projected line inside it; both bounds are parsed and retained on the model. ForecastDetails (web
    middle block) is a separate surface (own prompt) and is intentionally NOT rendered here.
  - States never hide a panel (TsEmptyState placeholders, never a blank box); freshness chip + refresh
    on the forecast panel header; reduce-motion honoured by TsFadeIn; Narrator names on surface/panels/
    charts/month-axis/refresh.

